{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Well the road was hot and flat as a ruler
Good [A]hundred miles between me and Missoula
That [B]vinyl top weren’t gettin’ no cooler
[B]So I stopped at a Quickie [E]Sack
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Cuz I figured I'd need about a six of Miller
And [A]one of them things so I wouldn't spill her
So [B]I asked the girl if the beer was in the back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
She said [B]"It's a dry town
No beer no liquor for [E]miles around"
I'd give a nickel for a [A]sip or two
To [E]wash me down [B]Outta this dry [E]town[A][E][B][E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
So I turn right around, no hesitation
Cursed the laws ruinin' the nation
Waved goodbye to the boy at the station
But she wouldn't go into gear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
He said it sounds like your transmission
You need to Bob, but he's gone fishin'
On his day off, he gets a long way from here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Well back home friends you can get a dose
Of something strong from a local grocer
So I walked down till I come closer
To a place called Happy Johns
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
He said "I keep something for colds and fevers
Down under here is where I usually leave her
But just last night I felt a cold a comin' on"
{end_of_verse}
